    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. AcceptanceTest is the only test class and both of its tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` derived field: **SILVER** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **BRONZE**.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` property (string enum `BRONZE`/`SILVER`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in the response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that derives the tier at response time:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()\n       ? OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.SILVER : OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.BRONZE\n   ```\n\nThe tier is computed purely from persisted owner state (`namesakeCount`, already stamped by `CountOwnerNamesakes` on create, and `email`), so it works identically on both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.",
